e Alzheimer disease, ADAS-cog 11 (0 to 70, higher is worse), trials of up to two years.","The marketed inhibitor's effect is the one fitted in the posterior itself (the manual's equation: effect at the reference dose times (dose / reference dose) to the fitted exponent), on the trials the model was built from; the range of the doses in those trials is not published in what this engine carries, so the same law is applied at any dose.","Against the Cochrane review of donepezil 10 mg at 24 to 26 weeks (Birks and Harvey 2018: -2.67 points, 95% CI -3.31 to -2.02) the fitted effect lands inside the interval. That is a check that the equation is implemented as published, not an independent validation: the review pools the kind of trials this model was fitted on."]}}}
